# Data schema

```mermaid
erDiagram
  USER ||--o{ ROOM_MEMBER : joins
  ROOM ||--o{ ROOM_MEMBER : has
  USER ||--o{ MESSAGE : sends
  ROOM ||--o{ MESSAGE : contains
  USER ||--o{ ROOM : creates
  MESSAGE |o--o{ MESSAGE : replies_to
  USER {
    uuid id PK
    string username UK
    string email UK
    string password_hash
    string display_name
    string avatar_url
    string bio
    enum status "online, away, offline"
    timestamp last_seen_at
    timestamp created_at
  }
  ROOM {
    uuid id PK
    enum type "direct, group"
    string name "NULL for direct"
    string description
    string avatar_url
    uuid created_by FK
    timestamp created_at
  }
  ROOM_MEMBER {
    uuid room_id PK, FK
    uuid user_id PK, FK
    enum role "owner, admin, member"
    uuid last_read_msg_id FK
    boolean is_muted
    timestamp joined_at
  }
  MESSAGE {
    uuid id PK "time-sortable"
    uuid room_id FK
    uuid sender_id FK
    uuid reply_to_id FK "nullable"
    enum type "text, image, file, system"
    text content
    string attachment_url
    timestamp created_at
    timestamp edited_at
    timestamp deleted_at "soft delete"
  }
```

## Relationships

- `USER` and `ROOM` are many-to-many through `ROOM_MEMBER`, which also stores per-user state (role, mute, read position).
- A `USER` sends many `MESSAGE`s; a `ROOM` contains many `MESSAGE`s.
- `MESSAGE.reply_to_id` references another message for threaded replies.
- `ROOM.created_by` references the creating `USER`.

## Indexes

| Index | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `MESSAGE (room_id, created_at DESC)` | Latest messages and infinite scroll |
| `ROOM_MEMBER (user_id)` | Rooms list for a user |
| `USER (username)`, `USER (email)` | Login and search (covered by UNIQUE) |

## Design notes

- Direct messages are `ROOM` rows with `type = 'direct'` and exactly two members. Enforce one room per pair with a `dm_key` column (the two sorted user IDs joined).
- Unread count = messages in the room newer than `ROOM_MEMBER.last_read_msg_id`.
- Use cursor pagination (`WHERE created_at < :cursor LIMIT 30`), not `OFFSET`.
- Write to the database first, then broadcast over WebSocket. Use Redis pub/sub to relay between servers, and Redis with a TTL for presence and typing state.

## Screen to table mapping

| Screen | Data |
|---|---|
| Login / signup | `USER` |
| Rooms list | `ROOM_MEMBER` + `ROOM` + latest `MESSAGE` + unread count |
| Chat room | `MESSAGE` (paginated), inserts, `ROOM_MEMBER.last_read_msg_id` |
| Profile | `USER` + counts from `ROOM_MEMBER` and `MESSAGE` |



